r side of the castle  kind of gradually curving down into the  hills of the trees that go around this  area and that's the general idea of how  I wanted to more or less divide the  landscape that's also why I won't go out  of my way to make the entire area just  one big clogged elven village because  the idea is to have most of the  buildings on this side and just make the  rest of the landscape some trees and  some other things that I can play around  with like waterfalls because well I can  take some inspiration from Rivendell as  well as inspiration from nemesis with  that and maybe a tree house that's  something I kind of want to get into if  I have some time left for it as well  though again I haven't really set this  so far but I'm obviously on a very  strict deadline with this project as  well so I'm kind of in a hurry with  getting this done and I felt that's  something that kind of plays along with  making this as well I added the tower  over here to this building to the left  just to add a nice little well not a  nice little a pretty big accents on the  building on the left here to make sure  that big castle doesn't look so alone  and to kind of have that transition into  the high peaks of the castle  and in front of this building I wanted  to have this kind of Hanging Gardens  idea by playing with the hillside here  but at the same time having some flat  space for flowers and trees to make it  all fancy so there's a few terraces over  here with these walls and little pots  between them building the division  between that's I actually worked on that  for quite a while there and skipped  forward just a bit to ending this little  house in here which it's going to be a  very simple house and it's not going to  actually have any walls it's just gonna  have some pillars around this but it's  gonna be nice to add a bit of extra  depth to this area and make sure that  this village is a bit closer to the path  and especially because it's pretty much  quite far ahead of the larger building  in the back it just adds a bit more  attempt to the town I felt that's just  the idea behind and in this house here  what's also kind of interesting about  this is that Rivendell really has liked  a lot of what you see of Rivendell is  the arches you don't actually see any  walls with windows in them if you look  from a distance you just kind of see  endless arches and pillars with roofs on  top of them and that's also the kind of  impression that I wanted to give with  many of these buildings but I didn't  want to quite go for that hence why I  wanted to have as many layers of  different arches as I could with as  little of the amount of space as I could  so while this building is still an open  work building you can actually see on  the building in the back I added those  long very tall arched windows behind  already-existing  while a double row of arches to kind of  give that idea of an endless Gaelic  gallery of arches and pillars without  actually having to make one and saving  myself at least a bit of time and  computer issues in the process and I'm  pretty happy with how that turned out  and a lot of this is also just  decorating the garden a little bit more  with some simple fences and flowers and  things like that  one of the issues that I do have with  this is that many of the details that  I'm well working with at the moment are  White's  and we can't recover anything in the  game so far  you more or less just had to work with  the colors that we have and kind of try  to fit different pieces together to get  slightly different color schemes but  there's no moving away from the color  schemes that we have at the moment is  even though we can make many shapes with  them that's just pretty much a given  right now and I wanted to bring back  those whites a little bit by just having  as much foliage as I can here and why I  didn't want to make these garlands  pretty densely foliage if that is a word  and edit all of these hanging baskets  and flower pots and planters things like  that all around these gardens and the  houses to add some greenery and more  color to these I also figured it would  be nice to make a quick custom little  shrub with the three branches actually  reckon they're really good for making  different kinds of shrubs I haven't  looked into it very much but you can  basically combine it with many of the  plants just use the driftwood and some  of the different plants elements and you  can actually make some really creative  stuff even well custom trees though  that's something that's for a well  future episode and I'm not going to  spoil that quite yet but I'm looking  into treehouses I kind of spoiled my  idea there anyway but yeah that's that's  the idea that I'm still looking into  anyway moving on to the last build of  this time-lapse and this is well  actually in the end it turned out to be  one of my favorites I didn't really  expect it beforehand I wasn't really  sure how this would turn out it's  basically going to be a small pavilion  if you know River now you know that like  pavilion that's down there with a lot  like openwork decorations on top of it  and it's that kind of idea which I  wanted to try here of course it's a bit  different and I really couldn't work  with the details that are used in  Rivendell given the pieces that we have  and the fact that many of the pieces are  quite clunky but I wanted to make a  classical pavilion with some pillars  around it and a dome on top of it over  here and this is basically my try at  doing so and for the openwork in the  middle just to make it more fancy and  more interesting and give it a bit of  density to the dome as well without  adding an actual roof because I think  especially openwork like this is  quite common for Alvin kind of  architecture so something I really  wanted to mess around with and even  though it turned out to be kind of hard  to cut these things into the exact  position that I wanted it's just gonna  make this don't look like it actually  has the shape of a dome and has some  interesting details of the roof while at  the same time keeping it see-through so  you can see the things behind it and it  doesn't really obstruct the view or  anything it still blends in quite nicely  with the pretty dense area around it as  well and that's the idea behind this  little preferring over here aside from  the obviously different term though it's  pretty similar to what I've already had  at this point in time it's just the dome  that's sort of like the new thing over  here I've also had the question of  whether I could make a bridge like the  one in River now if you know about River  now there's this bridge which shares the  roof design with the pavilion over there  which is a really cool bridge like it  has these very nice arches above it also  has arches underneath it and like big  waterfalls but that's just I guess just  on too big of a scale to really make it  happen here like I do still want to keep  it on a somewhat manageable scale but I  am in the end quite happy with how this  Bavarian turnouts also I do need to  preserve some space there's not a lot of  space left between the coasters hence  why I don't want to theme too much  between them simply because it's hard to  do so and much of the scenery is gonna  have to be just around these areas and  there's definitely no room around the  roller coasters to mess around with very  large bridges or anything like that and  another issue is that at this point I've  got so many sight lines that I kind of  want to keep around and kind of want to  keep open and pretty much safe from  foliage or buildings or anything that  could block the view that there are a  lot of like protected areas within this  valley that where I don't build anything  to prevent losing the view so there  aren't too many other areas where I'll  be building a lot so this village is  gonna set most of the scene in terms of  having buildings there are quite a few  that I still have like I already have  the castle and the station and there are  gonna be a few that I should hopefully  still plant around not to mention that  there are some flat rides as well but  this is gonna be most of it since much  of the focus is just on the roller  coasters themselves and like I said this  is more or less just the kind of  backdrop and scenery thing that I really  really wanted to try but it doesn't  exactly translate well into having it  around the roller coaster itself and  going to complicated into the scenery  and I'm finishing this off just a bit of  foliage around this area to make it look  a bit nicer I'll get into big forests on  those hills but this is just a quick  start and the small fence around here  anyway that is right about it's for the  time-lapse part today but I do still  have some cinematic shots saved so I'll  share those and with that I'm going to  end this video so thank you guys for  watching I hope to see you guys next  time
 

